sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant O as sender (holds messages:force)
  participant F as fleet (core)
  participant C as computer side (trierarch, or plugin watcher)
  participant H as plugin hooks
  participant A as agent session
  O->>F: send force=true
  alt sender lacks messages:force
    F-->>O: FORBIDDEN, nothing stored, key unused
  else reach refuses
    F-->>O: NOT_REACHABLE, refusal recorded
  else stored
    F-->>O: OK messageId (committed first)
  end
  Note over F: a pull ship (no computer side): force changes nothing, its next receive gets it
  C->>F: pushReceive
  F-->>C: deliveries, forced ones first
  alt turn idle
    C->>F: handed n
    C->>A: hand-over line as a prompt (as today)
    A->>H: UserPromptSubmit: ack, message into the turn
  else turn busy, trierarch session
    C->>A: interrupt key: the turn stops
    C->>C: marks the turn idle (it stopped it)
    C->>F: handed n
    C->>A: hand-over line as a new prompt
    A->>H: UserPromptSubmit: ack, message into the turn
  else turn busy, hand-crewed session (watcher cannot stop a turn)
    C->>F: handed n, kept in the store
    A->>H: next tool call (PreToolUse) or Stop
    H->>F: ack
    H-->>A: tool call denied with the message as reason, or turn kept open with it
  end
  alt the interrupt does not stop the turn within 10 s
    C->>A: types the line anyway: queued, the next tool call confirms it
  else ack refused or no answer
    H-->>A: shows nothing, stays received
    C->>F: handed n+1 at the next pass
  else session dies before the ack
    C->>F: died: handed again with the next number, the first prompt confirms
  else compaction
    Note over H,A: the store survives, the next prompt or tool call confirms, exactly once
  else lease ends
    F->>F: back to pending, attempts kept
  end
  Note over F: a forced delivery runs on the 10 minute clock, busy or not
